<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamburg is a major port city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> on the River <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>. As a free imperial city and member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>, it developed a commercial economy largely independent of imperial direction. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> it connected northern European markets with the Baltic and wider trade networks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamburg.jpg" alt="Hamburg" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dietmar Rabich · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamburg,_Landungsbr%C3%BCcken_--_2016_--_3131-7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
